Ace was only following my orders.

57
00:05:57,097 --> 00:05:59,177
Isn't that right, Marco?

58
00:05:59,177 --> 00:06:01,577
Yep, I heard it myself.

59
00:06:01,577 --> 00:06:02,537
Then you left.

60
00:06:02,537 --> 00:06:05,257
Sorry for all the trouble, really.

61
00:06:05,257 --> 00:06:09,097
Teach broke the rules of our ship, and you had to seek justice.

62
00:06:09,097 --> 00:06:12,857
Everyone in the world knows what happens if you mess with one of our crewmates.

63
00:06:12,857 --> 00:06:15,497
If you do, you're gonna pay the price.

64
00:06:15,497 --> 00:06:22,137
That means if anyone lays a finger on you, Ace, they're gonna have to deal with us!

65
00:06:22,137 --> 00:06:26,137
Don't worry, Ace, we'll get you out of here!

66
00:06:26,137 --> 00:06:36,777
Get ready to make hell your new home, Navy bastards!

67
00:06:36,777 --> 00:06:42,777
Have to admit, we asked for this.

68
00:06:42,777 --> 00:06:45,897
That had better not be regret, I hear.

69
00:06:47,817 --> 00:06:49,257
This is a real mess.

70
00:06:49,257 --> 00:06:55,417
All right, what do you say we tally up the odds?

71
00:06:55,417 --> 00:07:01,337
On this side, we've got us warlords, the Navy's most ferocious weapons, the admirals, and a hundred thousand soldiers!

72
00:07:01,337 --> 00:07:03,737
On that side, they've got the Whitebeard Pirates!

73
00:07:03,737 --> 00:07:06,537
An entire fleet of more than 40 allied ships.

74
00:07:07,177 --> 00:07:10,377
Okay, it's your move, Whitebeard. Let's go!

75
00:07:12,057 --> 00:07:14,217
Oh, I like it.

76
00:07:14,217 --> 00:07:21,177
Looks like you are gonna watch from the sideline.

77
00:07:21,177 --> 00:07:23,497
I know. You're just here to kill some time.

78
00:07:25,417 --> 00:07:26,617
More for me, then.

79
00:07:29,177 --> 00:07:32,137
This is oppressive. I can hardly stand it.

80
00:07:32,137 --> 00:07:35,737
These men are all the same. Disgusting, bloodthirsty beasts.

81
00:07:36,297 --> 00:07:38,377
In all my travels, I've only met one exception.

82
00:07:39,097 --> 00:07:52,537
Please stay safe, Luffy. For me.

83
00:07:54,777 --> 00:07:57,017
The water! What's wrong?

84
00:07:57,017 --> 00:08:05,897
It's receding. What's causing it?

85
00:08:09,577 --> 00:08:11,097
What the hell is going on?

86
00:08:12,217 --> 00:08:15,497
What's happening? Why is the ship moving backwards?

87
00:08:20,617 --> 00:08:25,817
Oh, come on! We had this! What gives? It was nothing but smooth sailing two minutes ago!

88
00:08:25,817 --> 00:08:27,177
I mean, it confuses you!

89
00:08:28,217 --> 00:08:30,537
Campbell, you've got some of my favorite parts there!

90
00:08:36,537 --> 00:08:39,337
Stupid ocean, we don't have time to go backward!

91
00:08:39,337 --> 00:08:40,617
What's making this happen?

92
00:08:42,537 --> 00:08:43,497
He's here.

93
00:08:55,817 --> 00:09:08,537
What? And now it's over? I'm not complaining, but weird.

94
00:09:08,537 --> 00:09:11,257
It pushed us! A good distance back.

95
00:09:11,257 --> 00:09:17,257
Well, great! At this rate, by the time we get there, the fight will be over!

96
00:09:24,537 --> 00:09:25,657
What was that?

97
00:09:25,657 --> 00:09:32,777
Jinbei! Come on! Can we go faster? We're already late! We can't let them kill Ace!

98
00:09:34,137 --> 00:09:37,817
Ace will be safe, for now. We'll get there.

99
00:09:37,817 --> 00:09:38,537
Okay.

100
00:09:39,497 --> 00:09:40,457
Give me a break!

101
00:09:43,577 --> 00:09:45,577
What? You know something that we don't?

102
00:09:46,617 --> 00:09:49,577
Is your fish man karate gonna get us there on time?

103
00:09:49,577 --> 00:09:53,817
Or better yet, are you gonna get your pals the whale sharks to give us a ride?

104
00:09:53,817 --> 00:09:56,217
My powers don't have much to offer here.

105
00:09:56,217 --> 00:09:58,617
Yeah? Then where's that confidence coming from?

106
00:09:58,617 --> 00:10:01,497
He says we'll make it, okay? So we're gonna make it!

107
00:10:01,497 --> 00:10:04,377
He says we'll make it! It's that simple, huh?

108
00:10:05,417 --> 00:10:06,937
Fine. You keep believing.

109
00:10:07,657 --> 00:10:08,937
I'm taking a nap.

110
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:12,057
Wake me when we get there.

111
00:10:12,057 --> 00:10:19,417
Uh, Captain Buggy? I really don't see this working out if we don't move any faster.

112
00:10:19,417 --> 00:10:24,137
You're not giving up on your dream, are you? To become the king? It's destiny, right?

113
00:10:24,137 --> 00:10:30,857
Oh, uh, yeah. Well, when the timing's right, I'm sure some kind of miracle will happen.

114
00:10:30,857 --> 00:10:34,537
But this obviously ain't the right time, so all I can really do is wait.

115
00:10:34,537 --> 00:10:38,777
So you are giving up? How can you let us down like that?

116
00:10:38,777 --> 00:10:40,617
What's wrong with you? Can't you see?

117
00:10:40,617 --> 00:10:46,297
Huh? Just look at him. That's not surrender. It's not laziness. That's confidence.

118
00:10:47,577 --> 00:10:50,057
No, it's not. Not at all.

119
00:10:50,697 --> 00:10:56,297
See? Cool as can be. He's perfectly composed. So regal he's like a king already.

120
00:10:57,417 --> 00:10:59,337
How can I be so blind? You're right.

121
00:10:59,337 --> 00:11:00,777
He's amazing!

122
00:11:01,497 --> 00:11:03,097
So wrong. All of it.

123
00:11:06,137 --> 00:11:09,977
I know miracles ain't exactly the most common of occurrences,

124
00:11:09,977 --> 00:11:15,657
but what the hell else could I do except wait for one? Damn it.

125
00:11:15,657 --> 00:11:23,337
The tide is changing course. We're moving forward again.

126
00:11:23,337 --> 00:11:25,337
Did you do something?

127
00:11:25,337 --> 00:11:33,017
Not me. All I've been doing is keeping us on course.

128
00:11:33,017 --> 00:11:35,017
It feels like it's starting to pick up speed.

129
00:11:35,017 --> 00:11:36,697
It's happening! He's right!

130
00:11:36,697 --> 00:11:40,697
I know! What is it? What's going on?

131
00:11:40,697 --> 00:11:44,697
Hey, Captain Buggy! It's happening just like you said!

132
00:11:44,697 --> 00:11:58,377
Look! The miracle you prophesied!

133
00:11:58,377 --> 00:11:59,497
What's going on? Huh?

134
00:12:02,297 --> 00:12:04,057
It's just a coincidence.

135
00:12:06,057 --> 00:12:09,337
I don't know what's going on, but it's our chance! Go!

136
00:12:10,057 --> 00:12:14,057
What did I tell you guys? All you gotta do is wait for the right time!

137
00:12:14,057 --> 00:12:16,937
And now that time is calling me to become the king!

138
00:12:16,937 --> 00:12:21,017
You're incredible, Captain Buggy! One of a kind!

139
00:12:21,017 --> 00:12:24,617
Yeah! Captain Buggy!

140
00:12:24,617 --> 00:12:27,577
Yeah! At this rate, we'll make it for sure!

141
00:12:33,257 --> 00:12:34,697
Hey! Behind us!

142
00:12:42,217 --> 00:12:43,337
Oh, hell no!

143
00:12:46,937 --> 00:12:50,617
I don't get it!

144
00:12:50,617 --> 00:13:17,577
I don't get it! Nobody is moving!

145
00:13:17,577 --> 00:13:20,857
Maybe they're just waiting for Whitebeard's command!

146
00:13:21,897 --> 00:13:23,097
I'm choking on the tension!

147
00:13:28,297 --> 00:13:31,257
What the? It reversed! The tide is rising again!

148
00:13:34,857 --> 00:13:36,137
Look! The horizon!

149
00:13:44,937 --> 00:13:46,777
What the? That's not right!

150
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:49,257
And here comes the final payoff!

151
00:13:49,257 --> 00:13:54,857
That harmless sea quake he threatened us with earlier was just the prelude to a massive tsunami!

152
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:06,457
The Quake Man is what they call him! He wields the power of the Tremor Tremor Fruit!

153
00:14:06,457 --> 00:14:08,217
The Tremor Tremor Fruit!

154
00:14:14,457 --> 00:14:20,137
Our forces may be many, but that won't guarantee a victory! Not against Whitebeard at least!

155
00:14:20,137 --> 00:14:28,617
Before him, before him, his crew, no one is safe! He has the power to destroy the world on his veins!

156
00:14:28,617 --> 00:14:38,297
It's happening! The Great War!

157
00:14:38,297 --> 00:14:41,097
It's happening! The Great War!

158
00:14:41,097 --> 00:14:42,777
Let's go!

159
00:14:42,777 --> 00:14:44,777
Let's go!

160
00:14:44,777 --> 00:14:46,777
Let's go!

161
00:14:46,777 --> 00:14:47,097
Yeah!

162
00:14:47,097 --> 00:14:48,777
Let's go!

163
00:14:48,777 --> 00:14:49,097
Let's go!

164
00:14:49,097 --> 00:14:50,777
Let's go!

165
00:14:50,777 --> 00:14:52,777
Let's go!

166
00:14:52,777 --> 00:14:53,657
Let's go!

167
00:14:55,817 --> 00:15:00,777
The Invaders! 47 pirate ships from the new world led by Whitebeard!

168
00:15:01,417 --> 00:15:05,097
The Defenders! The two greatest forces of the government!

169
00:15:05,097 --> 00:15:07,897
Navy HQ! And the Seven Warlords!

170
00:15:08,617 --> 00:15:14,457
No matter who wins, no matter who loses, the world will be forever changed!

171
00:15:14,457 --> 00:15:29,097
Let's go!

172
00:15:30,937 --> 00:15:31,497
Use thy solution!

173
00:15:37,417 --> 00:15:41,417
Pいきます!

174
00:15:44,457 --> 00:15:54,617
It's a Tsunami!

175
00:16:08,557 --> 00:16:10,497
Now that is power.

176
00:16:10,917 --> 00:16:12,657
He's straight out of hell.

177
00:16:14,457 --> 00:16:16,277
Ha! Ha! Ha!

178
00:16:40,237 --> 00:16:42,017
My sage.

179
00:16:42,017 --> 00:16:47,937
Aokiji, you little squirt.

180
00:16:48,497 --> 00:16:50,377
He froze it!

181
00:16:52,677 --> 00:16:54,757
That was too close!

182
00:16:55,257 --> 00:16:56,577
Kuzan saved our butts!

183
00:16:58,057 --> 00:16:58,937
Artisan!

184
00:16:58,937 --> 00:16:59,297
Artisan!

185
00:17:12,017 --> 00:17:37,477
The whole bay is iced over!

186
00:17:38,417 --> 00:17:39,577
The ship's locked in.

187
00:17:39,857 --> 00:17:40,717
We can't even move.

188
00:17:40,717 --> 00:17:43,737
Hey, come on, guys.

189
00:17:43,897 --> 00:17:45,437
We've got the admirals on our side.

190
00:17:45,557 --> 00:17:47,157
They're the Navy's greatest warriors, right?

191
00:17:47,897 --> 00:17:49,117
Yeah, you're right.

192
00:17:49,377 --> 00:17:50,777
There's nothing to be scared of.

193
00:17:51,217 --> 00:17:52,257
Screw Whitebeard.

194
00:17:53,477 --> 00:17:54,517
All cannons!

195
00:17:55,157 --> 00:17:56,077
Open fire!

196
00:17:56,257 --> 00:17:57,537
Save the Moby Dick!

197
00:18:10,717 --> 00:18:13,637
Well, let's move.

198
00:18:13,897 --> 00:18:15,437
We've got something to stand on now.

199
00:18:15,937 --> 00:18:18,117
Let's show them what we can do, gentlemen!

200
00:18:18,117 --> 00:18:28,457
We've got the commanders backing us up, too.

201
00:18:28,677 --> 00:18:30,917
Open fire and give them everything you've got!

202
00:18:30,917 --> 00:18:39,797
Round to camera offensive.

203
00:18:39,797 --> 00:18:40,297
Right!

204
00:18:40,297 --> 00:19:00,097
If I'm not mistaken, that's the fifth division commander, Flower Sword Vista!

205
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:09,657
Keep on your toes, Toshigi.

206
00:19:09,897 --> 00:19:12,697
The commanders aren't the only ones we've got to worry about here.

207
00:19:12,977 --> 00:19:16,437
Every one of these SOBs is a mighty soldier in his own right.

208
00:19:16,437 --> 00:19:19,857
Yes, yes, thank you, sir.

209
00:19:23,237 --> 00:19:25,497
This ice in the water ain't half bad.

210
00:19:28,197 --> 00:19:31,377
Nice of him to set up some stationary targets for us.

211
00:19:31,657 --> 00:19:34,577
Let's finish these ships off so we can invade the island.

212
00:19:34,577 --> 00:19:43,037
Yeah, I'm not sure it's going to be that easy.

213
00:19:52,797 --> 00:19:55,617
They're sending out the vice-admirals of Navy HQ.

214
00:19:57,617 --> 00:20:00,797
It's a rare sight to see them all lined up in a row like that.

215
00:20:00,897 --> 00:20:01,877
Ain't that cute?

216
00:20:01,877 --> 00:20:05,997
It's like they rolled out a buster call to greet us.

217
00:20:06,457 --> 00:20:07,117
Too bad.

218
00:20:07,457 --> 00:20:09,557
Because this time we're the ones doing the busting,

219
00:20:09,777 --> 00:20:11,697
as they're all about to find out.

220
00:20:11,897 --> 00:20:14,157
Hey, Tsuru, why don't you stand back some?

221
00:20:14,777 --> 00:20:17,637
Yeah, please, just leave this nonsense up to us.

222
00:20:17,897 --> 00:20:19,097
Have a nice cup of tea.

223
00:20:19,357 --> 00:20:20,037
Stay safe.

224
00:20:20,817 --> 00:20:23,457
Don't give me that, you condescending pricks.

225
00:20:23,657 --> 00:20:24,477
I'm fine.

226
00:20:25,197 --> 00:20:27,017
Besides, there's no place safe now,

227
00:20:27,377 --> 00:20:29,657
even if I swam all the way to the end of the sea.

228
00:20:31,877 --> 00:20:35,117
We're setting anchor here on the ice, boys.

229
00:20:35,737 --> 00:20:38,037
It's time to trounce those Navy sissies.

230
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:39,757
Now push for solid ground.

231
00:20:39,977 --> 00:20:40,297
Go!

232
00:20:41,497 --> 00:20:43,677
We're happy to give our lives for Pops.

233
00:20:43,837 --> 00:20:44,637
It'd be an honor.

234
00:20:45,097 --> 00:20:45,897
Bring it on, Navy.

235
00:20:46,277 --> 00:20:47,717
My men got nothing to fear.

236
00:20:47,917 --> 00:20:48,477
Enough talk.

237
00:20:48,797 --> 00:20:49,357
Let's go!

238
00:20:49,597 --> 00:20:50,237
Score, pirates!

239
00:20:50,777 --> 00:20:51,177
Yeah!

240
00:20:51,177 --> 00:20:51,377
Yeah!

241
00:20:51,377 --> 00:20:51,577
Yeah!

242
00:20:54,577 --> 00:20:56,997
Now, it all begins.

243
00:20:56,997 --> 00:21:12,657
Oh, man!

244
00:21:12,957 --> 00:21:13,357
Look!

245
00:21:13,897 --> 00:21:15,977
Is Dracula and Mihawk gonna make a move?

246
00:21:16,157 --> 00:21:17,357
Well, what do you know?

247
00:21:17,617 --> 00:21:19,237
That is mighty strange.

248
00:21:19,617 --> 00:21:21,577
So piqued his interest, did they?

249
00:21:21,997 --> 00:21:24,397
Hawkeye, finally willing to fight.

250
00:21:24,397 --> 00:21:27,517
You're gonna grace them with your sword for once.

251
00:21:38,637 --> 00:21:43,437
That icy gaze would leave even a seasoned warrior frozen dead in his tracks.

252
00:21:44,037 --> 00:21:45,957
Even with his blade resting upon his back.

253
00:21:46,537 --> 00:21:48,357
Who has the courage to stare him down?

254
00:21:49,237 --> 00:21:49,757
Hawkeye.

255
00:21:49,757 --> 00:21:53,537
Every swordsman worth their salt longs to cross blades with him.

256
00:21:54,117 --> 00:21:56,437
How else are we to find our worth but to do?

257
00:21:57,017 --> 00:22:01,297
Climbing the steps of glory with death nipping at our heels.

258
00:22:03,257 --> 00:22:05,017
Hey, that's the black sword.

259
00:22:05,197 --> 00:22:06,077
Quite famous.

260
00:22:06,717 --> 00:22:07,677
To be precise.

261
00:22:07,937 --> 00:22:08,197
Huh?

262
00:22:08,657 --> 00:22:10,377
It's named Night.

263
00:22:11,137 --> 00:22:13,177
There are only 12 like it in the world.

264
00:22:13,497 --> 00:22:15,177
They bear the highest grade.

265
00:22:15,177 --> 00:22:17,057
See the dark edge of the blade?

266
00:22:17,437 --> 00:22:18,197
The temper line?

267
00:22:18,417 --> 00:22:19,477
Its clove pattern?

268
00:22:20,177 --> 00:22:24,037
An ornate design suitable for only the greatest swordsman.

269
00:22:33,177 --> 00:22:34,477
It's Hawkeye!

270
00:22:34,477 --> 00:22:58,337
To be precise.

271
00:22:59,457 --> 00:23:01,217
What are these?

272
00:23:01,217 --> 00:23:11,337
The End

273
00:23:11,337 --> 00:23:14,757
Mihawk and Kizaru launch an attack against Whitebeard.

274
00:23:15,077 --> 00:23:17,337
Unfazed, his commanders leap into the fray,

275
00:23:17,537 --> 00:23:19,597
showing off their fearsome Devil Fruit powers.

276
00:23:20,037 --> 00:23:21,377
As the struggle rages on,

277
00:23:21,717 --> 00:23:24,197
Admiral Aka'inu unleashes a living hell

278
00:23:24,197 --> 00:23:25,977
that transforms the battlefield.

279
00:23:26,897 --> 00:23:28,277
On the next One Piece,

280
00:23:28,277 --> 00:23:30,137
an all-consuming Inferno,

281
00:23:30,137 --> 00:23:32,097
Admiral Aka'inu's power!

282
00:23:32,517 --> 00:23:34,317
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

